# --- registry -------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by setup/lib/models.sh (workloads_all) and setup/lib/budget.py
# (workload_plan). A workload is NOT a model profile: it is started by
# bench/sideserver.py as a transient unit with its own memory ceiling, never
# by llama-user@, and it appears in no Conflicts= line.
WORKLOAD_TITLE=SDXL-base 1.0 text-to-image via stable-diffusion.cpp (Vulkan)
WORKLOAD_KIND=image
WORKLOAD_MODE=batch
# The build is PINNED, not a symlink — the discipline flashnext.env applies
# to LLAMA_BIN, for the same reason: a figure measured on one build says
# nothing about another, and a symlink that moves turns every measured field
# below back into a claim. Built 01.09.2026 by setup/scripts/build-sd.sh.
#
# Vulkan first is a decision to be MEASURED, not a preference: the backend
# rule in docs/MODELS.md was derived from llama.cpp speculation workloads
# and says nothing about diffusion on gfx1151.
#
# The command is split on WHITESPACE by setup/lib/systemdfile.py — systemd
# EnvironmentFile syntax, no shell quoting — so nothing multi-word may live
# in it. The prompt is WORKLOAD_PROMPT below, appended as ONE argument by
# the runner; the output path is appended by the runner too (-o), because
# where a run writes belongs to the run, not to the profile.
#
# -H/-W 1024: SDXL's native resolution. --steps 30, --cfg-scale 7: the
# model card's defaults. --seed 42: fixed, so two runs of this profile are
# the same experiment. None of these is a measured optimum yet.
WORKLOAD_CMD=@HOME@/stable-diffusion.cpp/build-vulkan-6b3edaaf3/bin/sd-cli \
  -m @MODELS@/image/sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors \
  --vae @MODELS@/image/sdxl_vae_fp16_fix.safetensors \
  -H 1024 -W 1024 --steps 30 --cfg-scale 7.0 --seed 42 -v
# sdxl_vae_fp16_fix: the stock SDXL VAE produces NaNs in fp16; the fixed VAE
# (madebyollin/sdxl-vae-fp16-fix) is the established replacement.
WORKLOAD_PROMPT=a lighthouse on a rocky coast at sunset, detailed oil painting, dramatic clouds
# Every byte the job will load — the guard's estimate basis until the fields
# below are measured. Weights CreativeML OpenRAIL++-M (commercial use
# permitted), fetched 01.09.2026 from stabilityai/stable-diffusion-xl-base-1.0
# and madebyollin/sdxl-vae-fp16-fix.
WORKLOAD_FILES=@MODELS@/image/sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors @MODELS@/image/sdxl_vae_fp16_fix.safetensors
# WORKLOAD_SOURCE — where the weights come from, machine-readable
# (URLs, space-separated); fetched 01.09.2026. The prose history
# stays in the comments above; this line is for tooling and for
# the next machine. NOTE the VAE was RENAMED on download: the source
# basename is sdxl_vae.safetensors, the local file (WORKLOAD_FILES above)
# is sdxl_vae_fp16_fix.safetensors — a fetch tool deriving basenames from
# these URLs would stumble here (re-review, 01.09.2026).
WORKLOAD_SOURCE=https://huggingface.co/stabilityai/stable-diffusion-xl-base-1.0/resolve/main/sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors https://huggingface.co/madebyollin/sdxl-vae-fp16-fix/resolve/main/sdxl_vae.safetensors
# WORKLOAD_SMOKE_SHA256 — the DETERMINISM PIN: the exact output hash a
# 1-rep bench at this profile's settings on the pinned build must
# reproduce. tests/live_media.sh verifies it through the fence; a flip
# means build, weights or flags changed the output — the sharpest
# regression instrument this stack has. Re-declare on any deliberate
# change, with the report that measured it.
WORKLOAD_SMOKE_SHA256=a077e8556c4032d2e6b55c8489a11253cde7606ffba5c92baf12bc57e7f8bf27
WORKLOAD_SMOKE_SHA256_SOURCE=01.09.2026, rep1 sha256 of reports 0137/0239 (4 runs byte-identical across two process lifetimes)
# --- measured fields ------------------------------------------------------
# Born UNMEASURED on purpose. Until a first run under bench/sideserver.py
# fills them, budget.py charges the files plus its buffer term and says
# ESTIMATE out loud. Fill BOTH or neither, each with date + method, and say
# which machine (WORKLOAD_MEASURED_ON) — tests/test_workloads.py holds the
# contract.
#
# WORKLOAD_GTT_GIB        peak GTT the job pins (delta over the settled
#                         baseline while production is stopped)
# WORKLOAD_HOST_RSS_GIB   peak RssAnon of the process
#
# NOTE the estimate was LOW: files + buffer floor predicted 12.8 GiB and the
# observed peak is 13.1 — the buffer floor was calibrated on llama.cpp loads
# and a diffusion sampler allocates differently. The measured figure (plus
# budget's 10 % peak margin) is what guards now.
#
# First run also logged one WARN: "ggml_vulkan: Failed to allocate pinned
# memory (ErrorOutOfDeviceMemory)" during VAE decode — non-fatal, output
# verified sound (imagecheck: spread 62.3, r 0.99). If images ever come out
# broken, that warning is the first suspect.
WORKLOAD_GTT_GIB=13.1
WORKLOAD_GTT_SOURCE=01.09.2026, sideserver workload metering: peak of mem_info_gtt_used at 1 Hz minus the 0.7 GiB settled baseline, production stopped, one smoke run (30 steps, 1024x1024); the 3-rep bench re-read +13.14
WORKLOAD_HOST_RSS_GIB=5.0
WORKLOAD_HOST_RSS_SOURCE=01.09.2026, same run: peak RssAnon of the sd-cli process at 1 Hz; the bench re-read 5.04 summed over the unit cgroup
WORKLOAD_MEASURED_ON=gfx1151, 124.9 GiB RAM, build vulkan-6b3edaaf3
#
# COST, first bench (bench/reports/2026-09-01_0137_image_sdxl/): median
# 110.0 s per 1024x1024 image at 30 steps (min 109.85, max 110.38, n=3) —
# sampling ~99.7 s (3.3 s/step) plus VAE decode ~9.3 s, model load ~10 s on
# top of each CLI invocation. And DETERMINISTIC: all reps plus the earlier
# smoke run are byte-identical (sha256 a077e855…), across process
# lifetimes. That determinism is the sharpest instrument this stack has —
# a build A/B can diff hashes instead of statistics.
